## What this is

I authored a standalone deep correctness analysis of the post-PR-1 / post-PR-2 multi-analyzer
data flow as a new **§9** in `planning/multi-analyzer-dataflow-map.md` (branch under analysis:
`ta-anchor-refactor-v2 @ f6485980`, C1–C5 code-complete, local-only, unmerged). §9 is the durable
record; this handoff is the actionable notification. **I recommend; you decide/implement.** No
CURRENT.md change is requested here (that is why this is `plan__`, not `sync__`).

The full analysis (data-flow walk, branch/state matrix, fallback inventory, findings, scaling-case
walk §9.6, post-PR-2 end-state) lives at `planning/multi-analyzer-dataflow-map.md` §9.0–§9.6. This
handoff distils the decisions that bear on the coding plan.

## Headline — PR-1 survives all findings (Dean-directed, 2026-08-06)

**None of the §9 findings forces a code change into PR-1.** PR-1 can ship as-is. Reasoning (§9.4
"PR-1 survival gate"):

- **Every biting finding is confined to the opt-in configs** (`[sat,TA]` / `[TA]`-only). The default
  `[sat]`-only config is byte-identical to `main` (frozen by the #1513 goldens) and untouched by all of
  them. Even **VG-up** cannot fire in `[sat]`-only: a lone voter that is dead → nil anchor → whole
  optimize holds; live → no stale MAX contributor. VG-up needs *one live binder + one dead-but-enabled
  voter*, i.e. ≥2 analyzers.
- **Every biting finding fails toward over-provision or hold** — never under-provision or a crash.
  N3's missing nil-guard is **unreachable** in PR-1 (single pre-filtered caller, `rescale.go:307` under
  `applyRescale:225`).
- So the findings describe the safety/quality **envelope of the newly-enabled configs**, not a
  regression to the default.
- *Caveat:* default-config parity is proven only for the *all-live* decision set (goldens are all-live);
  the stale-`[sat]`-only path (dead sat → nil anchor → hold) is not golden-covered — the pre-existing
  `withSatEntry`-stability note, not a new blocker.

**Placement summary (which optional hardening lands where):**

| Item | Placement | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **VG-up** | **PR-1 close-out** (recommended) | one-liner; only scale-up-on-stale hazard; establishes the non-nil-anchor⟹non-empty-voting invariant PR-2 builds on |
| **VG-fallback + N8** | **PR-2** | same code site; the `.Live` one-liner is nearly vacuous; PR-2 completeness dissolves the fallback |
| **N2** (binder tie-break) | **PR-2** | unreachable in PR-1 (≤1 non-sat voter); becomes live when PR-2 admits multiple |
| **N7** (P/D role veto) | **PR-2** | multi-vote-combine semantics (abstain-vs-veto) |
| **N3** (rescale nil-guard) | optional / anytime | unreachable in PR-1; cheap hardening if desired |
| **N5** (Cost=0) | separate sat bug | pre-existing, all three configs |
| **N9** (reactive from-zero) | out of scope | pre-existing on `main`, untouched by PR-1 |

## Consolidates two already-.DONE handoffs

These two earlier planner handoffs raised pieces of the same gap and are already `.DONE`:
- `session/handoffs/plan__ta-anchor-live-flag-combine-gap.md.DONE`
- `session/handoffs/plan__ta-anchor-voting-liveness-gate.md.DONE`

This one **supersedes and consolidates** them into a single recommendation — do not treat it as a
