## Recommendation 1 — VG-up → PR-1 close-out (one-liner, ship-gate-safe)

**The gap (asymmetric).** `votingResults` (`analyzer_helpers.go:234-242`) prunes the ballot to
`e.Enabled` **only** — no `.Live`. The scale-up path consumes that slice (`initRoleState:271-307`
has no `.Live` guard; `roleBottleneckReplicas:326-342` takes a cross-analyzer MAX). So a
**dead-but-enabled** analyzer's stale `Result` can still **force a scale-up**. Scale-**down** is
already `Live`-gated (`needsScaleDownForRole:448`, `safeRemovalReplicasForRole:394` both
`if !e.Live { continue }`). Up unsafe, down safe.

**Recommended fix:** `votingResults:237` → `if e.Enabled && e.Live`. Because `initRoleState` /
`roleBottleneckReplicas` consume the pruned slice, this single change removes dead entries from the
entire scale-up path.

**Ship-gate safety.** The #1513 goldens (`[sat]`-only) and the Test 9 `[sat,TA]` combine
characterization fixtures are **all-live**, so the `.Live` predicate admits exactly the same set →
byte-identical covered behavior. The fix also establishes a clean invariant: **non-nil anchor ⟹
non-empty voting set** (the binder itself satisfies `Enabled && Live`). Degradation is correct: an
empty voting set → nil anchor → **hold**, never an unguarded scale-down. Suggested new test: a
dead-but-enabled entry asserting no scale-up from its stale RC.

**Scoping note (N4).** The scale-up replica **count** reads raw `e.Result` via `prcForVariant`, not
the anchor, so this touches the bottleneck count only through dead-entry removal; the anchor-derived
(b) value never reaches the count anyway.

**Why PR-1.** VG-up is the higher-severity of the voting-liveness pair (the actual
scale-up-on-stale-data hazard), it is independent of the PR-2 completeness work, and folding it into
PR-1 makes the non-nil-anchor⟹non-empty-voting invariant hold *before* PR-2 relies on it.
**Placement is your call**; the recommendation is PR-1 close-out.

## Recommendation 2 — VG-fallback + N8 → PR-2 (drop the fallback; revises plan V9)

**N8 — the sat (b)-fallback structurally lends only untrustworthy data.** The `bindingAnchor`
per-variant (b) fallback (`:208`, gated by `satEnabled := satNR != nil && satNR.Enabled`, `:169`,
no `.Live`) fires *iff* sat is `Enabled` but not binding — and sat binds *whenever*
`Enabled && Live && informative`. So its activation condition is *exactly* "sat is `!Live` **or**
non-informative," i.e. precisely when sat's (b) is untrustworthy. It can therefore only ever lend
stale or no-data/error sizing, and mixing it into a TA-bound anchor mixes the metric scale across
variants (the SOLE sizing-metric-mix site in the pipeline — see §9.6 scaling-case walk).

**Recommended: drop the (b)-fallback** — a binder-unknown variant keeps identity (a) but PRC=0
(abstain), matching `[TA]`-only. Byte-identical on the #1513 and Test 9 fixtures (sat binds in both →
fallback never fires), makes partial-from-zero consistent, and dissolves N1 + the fallback half of N5.
This **revises the FINAL plan's V9 enablement-gated-fallback choice**; it is Dean's design direction
(2026-08-06).

**Why PR-2, and the coherence caveat.** **VG-fallback and N8 are the same code site** (the `satEnabled`
gate). The `&& satNR.Live` one-liner is nearly vacuous (it removes only the `!Live` sub-case, leaving a
`Live`-but-non-informative sat still able to lend a stale stored PRC). So the two must move as a unit,
and PR-2 — where variant-completeness dissolves the fallback entirely — is the right home. **Do NOT apply
the vacuous `.Live` one-liner in PR-1**: half-fixing the site and then deleting it in PR-2 is churn. N8 is
not fail-dangerous (metric-mix → suboptimal sizing in an opt-in config, never a crash) and fires in neither
ship-gate fixture, so deferring it regresses no covered behavior.

## Recommendation 3 — two plan-affecting findings for PR-2

- **N2 — binder tie-break (latent, becomes live in PR-2).** `bindingAnchor` returns **nil** on
  `>1` non-sat `Enabled && Live && informative` binder (`:150`) → **permanent silent per-model
  hold** while the tie persists. Unreachable in PR-1 (≤1 non-sat voter); **PR-2 admits multiple
  voters**, so PR-2 must add a deterministic binder tie-break (e.g. sat-if-present, else lowest
  analyzer index).
- **N7 — divergent role decomposition vetoes per-role scale-down (P/D).** Role list =
  `rolesOf(anchor.VariantCapacities)` (from sat's (a) `.Role`), but `needsScaleDownForRole:451`
  requires **every live voter** to have `RoleSpare[role] > 0`. A live voter that decomposes roles
  differently — e.g. a non-disaggregated TA seeded with only a `RoleBoth` spare
  (`initRoleState:290-297`) — reads a map-miss on `prefill`/`decode` as `0.0` → **veto** → that role
  never scales down while the coarse voter is live. Reachable in `[sat,TA]` P/D. **Stuck-high, not
  unsafe.** Pre-existing combine property, but PR-2's multi-vote combine should decide whether a
  voter with no opinion on a role **abstains** rather than **vetoes**.

## Other findings recorded in §9 (context, no action requested)

- **N9 — reactive full-from-zero is budget-blind and wakes all variants.** The `scalefromzero` engine
  (`scalefromzero/engine.go`, a separate Runnable, `cmd/main.go:525-526`) has **no limiter** and scales
  every inactive VA `0→1` on EPP `pending>0` — no GPU/budget check, not cheapest-first (`:318` TODO).
  Pre-existing on `main`, untouched by PR-1, **not a PR-1 defect**; noted because it is the only path
  that wakes a *fully-cold* model under `[sat]`-only and bounds what anchor-side from-zero reasoning can
  assume (cold-start is budget-blind and non-cost-selective).
- **N1** corrects review finding **V6**: the (b)-fallback's real domain is the *opposite* of V6's
  claim — under the landed enablement gate it **never** fires in `[TA]`-only (`satEnabled=false`)
  and **does** fire in `[sat,TA]` when sat is enabled-but-not-binding. V6 must not be carried into
  the eventual §0–§7 migration.
- **N3** — `rescaleModelDecisions:342-344` dereferences the anchor with **no local nil-guard**
  (every sibling has one); safe today only via the `applyRescale:225-228` pre-filter (single caller,
  `rescale.go:307`) + `bindingAnchor` purity. **Unreachable in PR-1.** Latent fragility; cheap hardening
  = add the guard or compute-once-and-pass. Optional; any PR.
- **N5** — sat's `Cost=0`-for-zero-replica mis-ranking reaches **all three configs** (via the (a)
  merge onto TA's T-sfz PRC>0 variant → `costEfficiency=0` → ranked cheapest). Root fix is the
  separate sat `Cost=0` bug (out of scope for PR-1).
